    "probe": "ransom-note",
    "of": "examples/probes/ransom-note.json",
    "target": "Jamie Reid lineage: one slogan cut letter by letter out of other printed matter, mismatched size and face, torn edges, overprint",
    "method": "the same slogan, the same eight transforms, the same rngKeys. Three things are re-authored against default-v1: every cutting is now a seeded `tear` on a fragment clipped by a convex polygon, so it has two scissor edges and two torn ones; the misprint patch has moved on top of the cutting inside a `blend: multiply` group, so the red is a second impression rather than a shape behind the paper; and the nine faces on the sheet are nine real faces rather than two.",
    "notDone": "the newsprint ground is still the v0 field of rotring dots at density 19. `halftone` is a real screen but it is a whole-canvas two-tone stage, so screening this sheet would take the colour off the cuttings and off the overprint at the same time. The screen is tested on ransom-note-b instead, which is what pays for keeping it faked here."
  },
